Z||000005||FieroKyle||08-09-2001||12:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>(damned engine swap).[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>What kind of swap do you have in it???? I want to put a V-8 in mine eventually, so are you having troubles with your swap??? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Steve Normington||08-09-2001||01:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B> What kind of swap do you have in it???? I want to put a V-8 in mine eventually, so are you having troubles with your swap??? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aluminum head 3.4 out of a 1997 Olds Silhoutte. The aluminum heads require the use of the DIS instead of the distributor. The DIS requires the use of the Olds ECM and wiring. The Olds ECM and wiring requires the use of added electronics to defeat the anti-theft system and a special scan tool because the ALDL is gone. The aluminum heads also require custom welded alternator, compressor, and dogbone brackets because the bolt pattern on the side of the heads are different. If it weren't for the people on this forum, the Fiero would have had a tragic fire.||||reg||1
